* UPPR -- customer text upper-case converter demo. The COBOL program
* (runtime/cobol/uppr.cob) reads the operator's text from CUSTIN with
* RECEIVE MAP, folds a-z and the Latin-1 lower-case letters to upper
* case with INSPECT CONVERTING, and sends the upper-cased copy back in
* CUSTOUT.
MAP UPPR1 SIZE 24x80
  FIELD AT 0,0   LEN 42 PROT BRIGHT COLOR=BLUE      "UPPR -- Customer text upper-case converter"
  FIELD AT 2,2   LEN 50 PROT COLOR=TURQUOISE        "INSPECT CONVERTING: a-z and Latin-1 (äöü -> ÄÖÜ)."
  FIELD AT 5,2   LEN 22 PROT COLOR=TURQUOISE        "Customer text (input):"
  INPUT CUSTIN   AT 5,27 LEN 40 UNDERSCORE COLOR=GREEN
  STOP           AT 5,68
  FIELD AT 8,2   LEN 22 PROT COLOR=TURQUOISE        "Upper-case result:"
  FIELD CUSTOUT  AT 8,27 LEN 40 PROT BRIGHT COLOR=WHITE
  FIELD MSG      AT 11,2 LEN 70 PROT BRIGHT COLOR=YELLOW
  FIELD AT 22,2  LEN 30 PROT DIM COLOR=BLUE         "ENTER=Convert   F3=Exit"
  CURSOR         AT CUSTIN
ENDMAP
